From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:03:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/adbe: Queue the framebuffer hold work on system_dfl_wq

On the iPod touch 6 the first page flip warns "workqueue: work func
adbe_hold_work enqueued on deprecated workqueue": the flip path queues
the work on system_wq, which is being replaced. Nothing about the work
needs a particular CPU, so queue it on the unbound system_dfl_wq, from
both the flip and the work itself.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c
index ed033f3..0c7058f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c
@@ -712,8 +712,8 @@ static void adbe_hold_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	adbe_hold_release(adbe, false);
 	/* The newest entry is the one on screen: it stays until replaced. */
 	if (READ_ONCE(adbe->nhold) > 1)
-		schedule_delayed_work(&adbe->hold_work,
-				      msecs_to_jiffies(ADBE_HOLD_POLL_MS));
+		queue_delayed_work(system_dfl_wq, &adbe->hold_work,
+				   msecs_to_jiffies(ADBE_HOLD_POLL_MS));
 }
 
 /*
@@ -759,7 +759,7 @@ static void adbe_hold_push(struct adbe *adbe, struct drm_framebuffer *fb,
 				     "pipe not following updates, releasing the oldest held buffer\n");
 		drm_framebuffer_put(old);
 	}
-	mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &adbe->hold_work,
+	mod_delayed_work(system_dfl_wq, &adbe->hold_work,
 			 msecs_to_jiffies(ADBE_HOLD_POLL_MS));
 }
 
